 and military goods to  a war zone and we continue to supply  arms to ukraine we do this together and  we um actually exchange views on this in  order to bolster the defense of ukraine  against the russian invasions  and of course we need to do everything  in order to stop the senseless killing  and this is why call upon russia again  to finally agree to a ceasefire and to  withdraw its troops  we absolutely need to allow for  humanitarian access and  open safe corridors for people who want  to  leave and  we mustn't see military actions and have  bombings on refugees time and again this  war needs to stop  immediately a pivotal  and central element of our strategy is  to impose drastic costs  on russia for this war of aggression and  this is why it is right  that we have agreed in all the  structures that we are part of um to  impose sanctions that holds true for the  g7 we also talked about this in the  various phone calls that we had we other  partners together and we discussed this  within the framework of nato  finance industry we impose sanctions on  the financial sector on the financial on  the russian central bank an  extraordinary process that  we haven't  done  something that is unprecedented i'm  talking about sanctions on the russian  economy and these sanctions are highly  effective because indeed russia is  dependent on  imports in the field of technology  russia cannot replace these elsewhere in  the global markets and  europe and north america and japan south  korea many countries  that  gather as democratic states are those  who  have the best and the most  sophisticated technologies and of course  it is also important to affect and hit  the inner circle of the president and  the oligarchs and i explicitly want to  state this in london as well and i'm  grateful that the sanctions were widened  on many persons that are part of this  circle of people we have just accepted  and adopted a fifth uh sanctions package  within the european union  we're not 